From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:24:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(acnh): the text keyboard and the language list dock as
 one piece

At 0.92 the name entry's keyboard is docked to the picture's bottom; the
language list the globe key opens has to hold that dock. It fell back to the
middle for a moment, because the dock hung on the keys, which the list takes
away before its own rows are drawn, and the list's clip rectangles stayed
where the undocked list was, cutting the rows.

The dock is now the layouts' projection: while the keyboard or the list is
up, the screen UI manager's projection getter adds the picture's extra
half-height. Three stamps arm it (a key pane at state +0xb0, the list's
panes at +0x274, the dialog's name card at +0x1f0), and the dock holds 36
presents after the last of them, which carries it through the keyboard's
first frame and through the switch. The clip rectangles move with it, in
layout units. A 16:9 or 2.17 picture has no layout shift, so no stamp is
written and nothing changes there.

Checked headless on a Mac at 3.0.3 main with an island save: at 0.92 the
keyboard is at the picture's bottom from its first frame, the list keeps it
while the rows draw and while a language is chosen, and closing fades the
dialog out where it is; 16:9 and 2.17 are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: at 0.92 the name entry's keyboard is docked; the language list the globe key opens has to hold that dock. Between the keys' removal and the list's rows the interface fell back to the middle, and the list's clip rectangles stayed where the undocked list was, cutting the rows. The dock is now the layouts' projection, held for a moment after the last of three stamps, and the clip rectangles move with it in layout units
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the picture shape

